<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $24.27 bln on Dec 27.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $24.27 bln on Dec 27.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $24.27 billion on December 27, 1996 from $23.95 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Dec 27	Dec 20	 Dec 29</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,802	19,603	 17,467</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,347	 4,347	  4,429</p>
<p>    SDRs				   122	   --	     139</p>
<p>    Total			     24,271	23,950	 22,035</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
